    "explanation": "To both parties — the rider was overcharged, but by less than claimed; the driver's diversion is mostly, not fully, excused.\n\nTHE DEVIATION. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00104, weight 1.0) measures 34.17 km against the booked optimal of 27.1 km — an excess of 7.07 km, or 26.09%. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so a deviation is established. It is NOT material: 7.07 km is below the 8.0 km absolute test and 26.09% is below the 50% relative test. POL-RD-06 is therefore not engaged, so there is no repeat-pattern uplift and no driver-conduct referral. In any event the pattern test fails on the fields the clause names — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d of 288 (rate 0.003, far below 0.05). The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context-only under POL-GEN-01 and is not the field POL-RD-06 asks for; it was correctly not used as a ground.\n\nWHAT IS EXCUSED. LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20260716-007 (EV-ADVIS-00104-01, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) names the Pan Island Expressway towards Tuas after the Eunos Link exit — the very road and segment the optimal route uses — and its 20:02–21:35 window overlaps the trip (53.1 min). The trace shows the vehicle leaving the PIE at Bedok North Ave 4 before the blocked stretch and rejoining the westbound corridor after it. POL-RD-03 is satisfied. The excused excess is capped: min(7.07, 1.30 x (30.1 - 27.1) + 1.00) = min(7.07, 4.90) = 4.90 km. The driver's 34.17 km is 4.07 km longer than even the shortest lawful alternative (30.1 km), and that overrun beyond the cap is his to answer for. The second, operator-entered CTE advisory (EV-ADVIS-00104-02, weight 0.25, issue codes ADVISORY_UNCORROBORATED and UNVERIFIED_SOURCE) describes a corridor this trip never enters and carries nothing; the finding does not rest on it and is unaffected by its discount.\n\nTHE REFUND. POL-RD-02 runs against the closure-adjusted optimal: distance 27.1 + 4.90 = 32.00 km; duration 34.0 x (32.00/27.1) = 40.1 min. recomputed_fare = 3.80 + 0.75 x 32.00 + 0.28 x 40.1 + 0.80 platform fee = 39.828. charged_total = 43.41. refund = 43.41 - 39.828 = 3.582, rounded UP to SGD 3.60. That is not de minimis (above SGD 0.50) and well short of the 90% full-refund share, so it is a partial refund.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. The rider's fallback — that limb (c) of POL-RD-03 fails because the trace rejoins on the AYE and not the PIE — is rejected: the evidence records the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoining it after, which is what limb (c) requires, and nothing shows the vehicle simply drove an unrelated trip. On the rider's reading the refund would be 43.41 - 34.445 = 8.965, i.e. SGD 9.00 against the booked optimal; that reading is not adopted. The chat log (driver announcing the diversion, rider replying 'ok but not too long ah') is not a rider-requested detour: no waypoint_hint and no road named, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run, the clause is unavailable, and the case is decided on the remaining clauses — no excess is excluded on that ground. No pickup or dropoff amendment exists on the trip record, so POL-RD-05 does not run and the baseline stays the booked 27.1 km. There are no ERP or toll lines and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top of the POL-RD-02 figure.\n\nNO ESCALATION. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes (100% coverage, 283 fixes at 10 s, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; identifiers (TRP-00104) and timestamps match; no charge line lacks a counterpart; and the refund is far below the ceiling. No clause produces a referral."
